 "title": "WORD FORMATION ANALYSIS IN DENDRONYMS: A CASE STUDY OF THE GERMAN AND UZBEK LANGUAGES",
 "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/19340614",
 "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19340614",
 "description": "<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong>This article is dedicated to the morphological, semantic, and toponymic analysis of dendronym formation in Uzbek and German languages. Dendronyms &mdash; place names derived from tree or plant names &mdash; reflect national linguistic mentality and cultural identity. The paper outlines the affixal, compositional, and semantic derivation methods using concrete examples, and provides a comparative overview of both language structures.</p>",
